WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.235
-Our first guest is a Grammy-
and Emmy-winning comedian

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:06.372
who has a new podcast called
"The Midnight Miracle,"

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.908
which Is available now
on Luminary.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.178
Please welcome the one and only
Dave Chappelle!

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:16.783
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh!

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.219
Yes!
Dave!

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.520
-What's happening, Jimmy?

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.156
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.424
It is great to see you.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.194
-It's great to see you.
I'm sorry I'm not there.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.129
I didn't know you guys
were doing in-studio stuff.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.632
I'd have pulled up.
Shout-out to Steve Higgins.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.600
Shout-out to The Roots.
-There you go, yeah.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.502
Absolutely.
We're happy you're here.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.938
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.607
When everything closed down,
you were the first

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.745
of the comedians to do outdoor
socially distant shows.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.281
-Yeah, couldn't wait.
-I mean, it wasn't just comedy.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.950
There was music, too.
But what made you want to do it?

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.254
-You know, a lot of it started
when the protests started,

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.356
the George Floyd of it all.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:00.359
-And, boy, I really missed
having a microphone in my hand

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:04.931
when something like
that tragic happens.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.401
And so, the first night,
I had to call the governor,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.235
Governor DeWine,
to get an approval,

00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:12.272
which he luckily gave us.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.940
We had 60 people
in a 5-acre corn field,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.712
and we ended up doing about
54 shows in 15 weeks.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.048
-That's amazing.
That is unbelievable

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.516
that you pulled that off.
-And I got to say --

00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:27.186
I got to shout out --
Like, a lot of great comedians

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:30.423
came out here
and donated their talents.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.124
And it was just great
being with everyone

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.027
after being quarantined.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.263
And a shout-out to everyone who
came, because it was wonderful.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.132
-Please tell me
you documented some of this.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:43.036
-Oh, yeah, I documented
all of it, very thoroughly.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.105
-Oh, good, good, good.
-So, the very first night,

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.408
I had called my neighbors
just so I could film it.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:52.111
Just for, like, you know,
posterity's sake.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.981
And that first night
ended up being that set

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.716
that I released "8:46."

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:00.887
My neighbors, Steve Bognar
and Julia Reichert,

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:04.490
they won an Oscar last year
for a great documentary,

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.459
"American Factory,"
that the Obamas produced.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.162
-Oh, yeah.
-And I see them all the time

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.530
at the grocery stores
and everything,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.565
and I literally just
knocked on their door.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.034
We sat down and talked about it.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.637
So they ended up
filming all 54 shows.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.039
It was amazing.
-No way.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.808
So you have all of them?
-It was great.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.576
-Wow!
That's -- That's --

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:29.882
That special you did
was so needed and so powerful.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.218
Did you feel
how powerful it was?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.487
-It was a weird process.
I didn't expect that I would

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.123
put anything out,
but it became a thing

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:40.827
where I wouldn't feel right
telling jokes

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.061
until I addressed that,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.864
'cause people
listen to me different.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.800
And that was one of those
moments where I understood that,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.603
and we let it rip.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.572
So it was gut-wrenching
putting it out.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:53.873
To be honest,
I was real nervous about it,

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.975
but I'm glad that I did.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:59.812
-Yeah, we all needed it.
Clearly, the world needed it.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:04.684
Because it's the number-one
video on YouTube from 2020.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:07.854
-I beat a dancing squirrel
with that video, bro.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.455
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:13.859
-That's a very close second,
but you got the title.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.962
-Take that, squirrel.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:20.466
That's a pretty funny video,
that squirrel.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.902
Also, you know, I follow you
on social media even though

00:03:23.902 --> 00:03:26.905
you don't really post things
on social media.

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:28.541
-No.
-No.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.143
Like, Twitter,
I think the last time

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:33.212
you posted was
2012 or something.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:35.448
-Twitter is a bathroom wall.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.784
-I totally agree.
It is.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:43.022
-Why would I write all my
thoughts on a bathroom wall?

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.624
Donald Trump, you heard that?

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:48.294
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.929
-That's right.
[ Applause ]

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.264
-And don't cut that [bleep]
in post, Jimmy.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.767
-No, I don't -- I don't --

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.669
I don't cut
any of that stuff, man.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.806
I -- What?

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.507
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.576
-I was gonna do a joke
about drawing a [bleep]

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.678
on a bathroom wall.
-All right, all right.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.446
We'll cut that, we'll cut that.
-Cut that in post.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:10.015
-We'll cut that one, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.517
We'll cut the [bleep].
We'll leave the Trump.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.319
I know.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.821
Cut the [bleep]
He said cut the [bleep]

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.988
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.156
-I didn't say it.
I didn't say it.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.991
We're gonna cut that.
No one will ever see it.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.559
That's something
just me and you experienced.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.328
That never happened. No one
will ever know it happened.

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:26.832
So, anyways, you posted a video
called "Unforgiven."

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:31.004
You asked your fans to boycott
"Chappelle's Show," your show.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.471
-Yeah.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:35.408
-What happened,
and how did that all work out?

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.643
-Well, without going
into too much detail...

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:40.480
-Yeah.
-...that [bleep] worked.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.750
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.087
-Yeah. So, I think you have to
go into a little more detail.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.723
-All right, all right.
First of all,

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:54.426
shout-out to everybody
that helped me out with that

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:56.295
by not watching the show.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:57.696
Shout-out to Ted Sarandos,
that runs Netflix,

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:01.567
because he had the courage
to take off "Chappelle's Show"

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:05.772
from the platform at financial
detriment to that company,

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:08.807
and it opened the door for us
to resolve a longstanding issue.

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:13.112
And shout-out to Chris McCarthy
at CBS-Viacom because that guy

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.615
really did work hard with me
to make this thing right,

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:18.017
and he was wonderful
to work with on that.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.820
-Yeah, you didn't have
any of the rights

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.191
or anything to your material,
to what you were doing.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.325
Something like that?
-Something like that.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.360
-Yeah, I gotcha.
-Something like that, yeah.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.162
But all's well that ends well.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:32.632
I do now, so, please,
by all means, watch it.

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.032
-Oh, there you go, yeah.
So please watch.

00:05:34.032 --> 00:05:35.334
Watch "Chappelle's Show."

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:39.539
It's on every streaming platform
that you can think of.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.540
-And I'm very grateful, man.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.811
Like, people who --

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.645
People are wonderful to me.

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:49.481
That was -- That was --
I was very moved by the response

00:05:49.481 --> 00:05:53.218
of that and the support
that I got from people all over.

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:55.220
And I just want
to say thank you.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.924
If you're watching,
it meant more

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.525
than you could ever imagine.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.762
-Oh, we love you.
-I love y'all.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.331
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We do.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.966
-I love you, yeah, I do.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.968
-We want to talk about your
new podcast when we come back.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.871
More with Dave Chappelle after
the break, ladies and gentlemen.

